BT /F1 12 Tf 50 720 Td 16 TL (CHAPTER 1: PHOTOSYNTHESIS OVERVIEW) ' (Photosynthesis is the fundamental biological process by which green plants,) ' (algae, and cyanobacteria convert light energy into chemical energy.) ' (This chemical energy is stored in carbohydrate molecules such as glucose.) ' (The chemical equation for oxygenic photosynthesis is:) ' (6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy -> C6H12O6 + 6O2.) ' (The green pigment chlorophyll absorbs blue and red wavelengths of light.) ' ET
endstream
endobj
