BT /F1 12 Tf 50 720 Td 16 TL (CHAPTER 2: LIGHT REACTIONS AND THYLAKOID MEMBRANE) ' (The light-dependent reactions take place on the thylakoid membrane inside chloroplasts.) ' (During this stage, photons strike photosystem II, splitting water molecules through photolysis.) ' (This releases protons, electrons, and free oxygen gas as a byproduct.) ' (Electrons move through an electron transport chain to produce ATP and NADPH energy carriers.) ' ET
endstream
endobj
