9 0 obj
<< /Length 438 >>
stream
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 720 Td 16 TL (CHAPTER 3: CALVIN CYCLE AND CARBON FIXATION) ' (The Calvin cycle takes place in the stroma of the chloroplast.) ' (It uses the ATP and NADPH synthesized in the light reactions to convert CO2 into glucose.) ' (The enzyme RuBisCO catalyzes the initial carbon fixation step with ribulose 1,5-bisphosphate.) ' (Temperature, light intensity, and CO2 concentration are the primary factors affecting the rate.) ' ET
endstream
